  "title": "Kourovka problem 11.51 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Are there (large, non-trivial) classes X of torsion-free abelian groups such that\nfor A, C ∈ X the group Ext (C, A) is torsion-free? It is a fact (E. L. Lady, A. Mader,\nJ. Algebra, 140 (1991), 36–64) that two groups of such a class are nearly isomorphic\nif and only if they have equal p-ranks for all p.                              A. Mader",
